//! R8 — DE-MODELING B3: the REAL FVAR BINDER-OPENING DISCIPLINE, native == JIT
//! (Rust -> MIR -> trust-ir -> trust-cg -> machine code). The landed R6
//! flagship (`e2e_universe_realnames.rs` — untouched as the de-Bruijn-model
//! record) re-verified with its B3 model REPLACED by the production
//! clean-kernel binder discipline:
//!
//!   * `LocalContext`/`LocalDecl` (tc/local_context.rs) — the production
//!     context: Vec<LocalDecl> stack + the MONOTONIC `next_id: u64` fresh-
//!     FVarId counter (ids never reused after pop — invariant #1773), decls
//!     carrying {id, name: REAL Name, type_: Expr, value: Option<Expr>, bi}.
//!   * infer_type's Lam/Pi/Let arms run the PRODUCTION open→infer→close:
//!     ctx_push(Name::anon(), domain, *bi) → open_bvar (= instantiate with
//!     FVar — tc/eta.rs:197) → infer the CLOSED opened body → ctx_pop →
//!     abstract_fvar (Lam rebuild, expr/subst.rs Abstractor) / subst_fvar
//!     (Let zeta, FVarSubst). The FVar arm is the context lookup; the BVar
//!     arm is the production HARD ERROR (no de-Bruijn walking anywhere).
//!   * check_decl_readonly §5+§7 share ONE context (one per-call TypeChecker
//!     in production) — the FVarId counter continues across the steps.
//!
//! WHAT IS VERIFIED native==JIT here:
//!   * the R6 16-case decl-gate set re-run THROUGH THE FVAR PATH — same 6
//!     accepts / 10 rejects, error payloads deep-compared (REAL-Name payloads
//!     raw-decoded + per-node hash-chain revalidated, universe payloads
//!     structural, expr payloads meta-bit-identical at every node) — PLUS
//!     two FVar-specific cases: 16 "def.zeta" (ctx_push_let + FVar-typed λ
//!     domain + OBSERVABLE zeta subst inside a rebuilt Pi) and 17
//!     "def.shadow" (two binders BOTH opened as Name::anon(); the body
//!     references the OUTER one — lookup must scan past the innermost decl;
//!     correct iff the ids are fresh). 8 accepts / 10 rejects total.
//!   * the FVar-discipline probes: stale-FVar `UnknownFVar` production-error
//!     identity (empty ctx / popped decl / nonempty-missing-id), monotonic
//!     no-reuse after pop (pop then push mints id 1, never 0), the shadow
//!     open→infer→close replay with IN-MODULE-asserted DISTINCT fresh ids,
//!     the abstract_fvar↔instantiate round-trip (structural + meta-bit
//!     identity + FVar-erasure), and a dependent Pi whose body sort requires
//!     the opened FVar's context type.
//!   * NEGATIVE CONTROLS: the ARMED id-collision control (probe 4 forces the
//!     second open to REUSE id 0 via the clearly-marked non-production
//!     `push_forced_id_control`): the production freshness guards trip
//!     (guard_trips == 2, the two would-be assert! failures) and the rebuilt
//!     type DIVERGES (…Sort u → …Sort v, pinned to the kernel `v` golden) —
//!     freshness is load-bearing AND observable, deterministically, native ==
//!     JIT on the broken path too. Plus the armed module-text corruption
//!     (`const u64 1723` → 1724 — the anon hash seed in name_anon's machine
//!     code): every constructed Name hash diverges EXACTLY as predicted
//!     (mix(1724, murmur("u",11))), proving the hash chain truly runs in the
//!     JIT machine code. Plus the R6-style always-accept / meta-corruption /
//!     crossed-universe comparator controls.
//!
//! Modeled boundaries (full list in the slice header): B1 env slice-scan,
//! B4-B11 as R6, [C-refcell] RefCell→&mut threading, [C-idx] HashMap index →
//! backward scan, [C-guard] freshness assert! → guard_trips counter. B3 is
//! CLOSED for the inference surface. B7 note: meta payload hashes still run
